searchfire: answer a multi-question query with few, paced packets

A Dante receiver refreshing its cache asks about every channel in one query
(60+ questions, every ~96 s at 80 % of the 120 s TTL). searchfire answered
each question with its own packet: 60+ multicast packets in ~3 ms. On a
100 Mbit port that burst queued ~2.5 ms in front of the audio, and an ESP32
receiver at 1 ms latency dropped 4-8 packets on every refresh.

Now all matching services are merged into one response, duplicates (the
shared host A record) dropped, split at 1400 B and sent 1 ms apart. The
start-up announcements go out the same way. 64 channels: 8 packets instead
of 64. Same fix as osx.N-Series.AoIP a9a3081.

